  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is driven by three primary failure modes: mid-day liquidity droughts (10:30\u201311:15 IST entries on 2026-10-22 in TATASTEEL, AXISBANK, and NTPC) where 2.0x volume sweeps lacked institutional follow-through and reversed into tight 0.45%\u20130.50% stops; late-afternoon entries (14:25\u201314:30 IST in COALINDIA and ICICIBANK) that ran out of session time to hit the ambitious 1.2% target, resulting in stagnant EOD square-offs eroded by brokerage/STT fees; and premature trailing stop triggers (Trade #2 ICICIBANK) where a gross profitable move turned into a net loss due to transaction cost drag. Notably, total gross P&L across the 12-trade sample was positive (+\u20b926.94), proving that directional edge exists but is currently being cannibalized by \u20b943.40 in fee friction and noise-band stop-outs.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a \u20b910,000 micro-capital base, statutory and brokerage fee drag (~0.15%\u20130.20% round-trip) severely penalizes stagnant late-session trades and scratch exits; surviving intraday mean-reversion noise requires higher-conviction volume anomalies (\u22652.4x) paired with wider initial structural stops (0.55%) and more achievable profit targets (1.0%) that capture momentum before the mid-day European-open lull or EOD square-off.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.0,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.4,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.15,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #59 Post-Mortem & Parameter Evolution\nIn Cycle #59, the DeepSeek V4.1 Flash out-of-sample run generated a positive gross P&L (+\u20b926.94) across 12 trades, but finished net negative (\u20b9-16.46, PF 0.81) due to \u20b943.40 in transaction costs and a cluster of mid-day false breakouts on October 22. Forensic analysis revealed that `min_sl_pct` at 0.45% sits inside normal 5-minute NSE order-book noise for high-beta names like TATASTEEL and NTPC, while `min_target_pct` at 1.2% proved too distant for afternoon setups (COALINDIA, ICICIBANK), forcing flat EOD square-offs that bled fees. To transition gross alpha into net profitability, we are widening `min_sl_pct` to **0.55%** to survive routine post-sweep retests, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to **2.4x** to filter out low-conviction mid-day head-fakes, lowering `min_target_pct` to **1.00%** to lock in clean intraday impulse waves before EOD decay, and shifting `breakeven_trigger_r` to **1.15R** to prevent premature scratch exits that lose money to fee drag."
